# The licensed Magma tarball, and the ad-hoc local setup around it.
#
# magma.tar.xz is commercial licensed software: never commit it, and never push
# an image containing it to any registry.
#
# These patterns are root-anchored on purpose. Unanchored patterns match at every
# depth, which previously hid tools/magma-docker/Dockerfile -- the committed,
# reproducible build recipe -- from git entirely.
/magma.tar.xz
/Dockerfile
/docker-compose.yml
/run-magma.sh
/run-magma-patched.sh

# Rust build artifacts are ignored by the submodule itself (rust/.gitignore),
# not from here: superproject ignore rules do not apply inside a submodule.

# Per-tester logs written by test_all.sh
.test-logs/

# Generator output from whitebox_auto_NEG.py. It writes beside the committed
# whitebox/logs/*.txt rather than over them, because those are the residue of the
# old orchestrator run and are the only record of how it behaved.
whitebox/logs/*.new

# Regeneration logs for the genus-2 ramified families. The committed logs in
# whitebox/logs/ are 44K-616K; a full run for these families is ~42M, because the
# generator's search loop keeps emitting long after it has covered every branch.
# Too large to track, and reproducible from the generator.
whitebox/logs/*_ramifiedG2_log.txt

# Regeneration logs for the genus-3 ramified families, 2.7M and 3.7M against a
# 616K largest-committed. Same reason as the genus-2 ramified ones, and these are
# strictly reproducible: their generators enumerate rather than search, so a run
# is a function of (WB_SEED, budget) and both are recorded in each generator's
# header. The committed logs above are kept only because they are the sole record
# of how the retired orchestrator behaved -- that is history, not a convention to
# follow for a new family.
whitebox/logs/*_ramifiedG3_log.txt

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the verification harness
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generator staging. A tester is of record once copied next to its formulas.
whitebox/testerFiles/
